WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.540
Speaker 1: Democrats are increasingly turning,&nbsp;
some are saying, on Democratic Senator from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:13.260
California, Dianne Feinstein, and demanding that&nbsp;
she resign. Let me remind everybody what is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:19.320
on. And there's a lot of sad stuff going on in&nbsp;
this story. Dianne Feinstein is currently the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:27.060
longest serving member of the U.S. Senate. She is&nbsp;
89 years old. She is she has announced she is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:34.200
seeking reelection in 2024. There have been many&nbsp;
concerns. I want to be as respectful as possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.640
but also be accurate. There have been&nbsp;
many concerns for years now about Dianne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:44.040
Feinstein's cognitive state. There are&nbsp;
public examples. Tough to watch, I admit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.980
Public examples of Dianne Feinstein asking a&nbsp;
witness during a Senate hearing a question.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:55.860
Hearing an answer from the witness and then&nbsp;
looking down at her papers and asking the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:00.120
exact same question a second time, seemingly&nbsp;
forgetting that she just asked that question.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:07.380
There are endless reports from staffers and&nbsp;
people in D.C. who work at the Senate saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:12.000
Dianne Feinstein regularly will meet someone that&nbsp;
she has met many times before, even recently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.800
and has no recollection of having met that&nbsp;
person. So. Listen, I mean, we don't have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.540
diagnosis here, but there have been concerns for&nbsp;
years about this. As far as Dianne Feinstein goes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:28.020
it is the right decision at this point. She had a&nbsp;
great run to not run for reelection in 2024. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:35.940
has surfaced in the wake of this is that there is&nbsp;
a primary in California in which three members of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:40.860
the House of Representatives have decided to&nbsp;
run for Dianne Feinstein Senate seat. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:45.540
Adam Schiff, who we've interviewed, Barbara Lee,&nbsp;
who we're going to interview, and Katie Porter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:50.820
who we would like to interview, but so far has&nbsp;
not responded to our requests. You can't run for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:56.040
House and Senate at the same time, meaning that&nbsp;
while all three of them, Barbara Lee, Adam Schiff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:02.400
and Katie Porter, who are mid-seventies early&nbsp;
sixties and around 50 years old respectively,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:09.480
while they are all competing for the Senate&nbsp;
seat, their congressional seats are now going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:14.940
to be open because they can't run for both at&nbsp;
the same time. Dianne Feinstein, on top of this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:21.960
as is reported by Newsweek, has recently been out&nbsp;
with shingles. And this is particularly impactful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:27.600
because Dianne Feinstein is on the Judiciary&nbsp;
Committee. And when you have such a divided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:33.600
government the way we have right now, where&nbsp;
Democrats barely control the Senate, judicial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:40.140
appointees are one of the relatively few ways that&nbsp;
Democrats can assert power, use their majority,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:48.120
and try to assist Joe Biden in getting things done&nbsp;
because of Dianne Feinstein's absence from that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:53.220
committee. It has effectively made it impossible&nbsp;
for Senate Democrats to continue confirming Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.220 --> 00:03:01.260
Biden's judicial nominations. So both because it&nbsp;
would potentially allow a different dynamic in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:06.840
the primary, which would be better for Democrats&nbsp;
and because of this issue on the Senate Judiciary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:12.840
More and more Democrats are saying that Dianne&nbsp;
Feinstein should resign right now. If Dianne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.680
Feinstein did resign and Farron Cousins talked&nbsp;
about this one filling in for me last week,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:21.540
to some degree, the governor of California,&nbsp;
currently Democratic Governor Gavin Newsom, would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:29.580
get to replace appoint a replacement to fill the&nbsp;
vacancy. Now, you have to understand that there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:35.280
are different dynamics in California depending on&nbsp;
how long it is until the next general election. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:41.460
Dianne Feinstein were to resign within six months&nbsp;
of the general election, there wouldn't be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:49.140
special election for the seat. You would just wait&nbsp;
until the general election. When you have under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:55.080
I'm sorry, when you have more than 180 days left,&nbsp;
then you would do a special election. Right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.080 --> 00:04:02.160
because we have more than 180 days until the 2024&nbsp;
election. If Dianne Feinstein resigned today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:07.680
you would see the appointment by Gavin Newsom&nbsp;
and then you would see a special election that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:12.780
is potentially a much better path forward, both,&nbsp;
number one, because of its impact on the Senate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:17.580
Judiciary Committee. And number two, because&nbsp;
it might actually change the game with regard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:22.020
to so many Democratic open seats in the House of&nbsp;
Representatives that increasingly Democrats are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:28.320
saying that is exactly what should be done. It&nbsp;
doesn't appear as though right now there is big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.820
momentum for Dianne Feinstein to actually do&nbsp;
that. And it's unclear whether that is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:37.560
to change. The other aspect to this that's being&nbsp;
discussed is what about appointing a replacement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:42.720
on the Judiciary Committee for Dianne Feinstein?&nbsp;
I don't have a lot of news to give you about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:48.780
that right now, but it is certainly something&nbsp;
that is being discussed. My leaning right now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:55.260
Is that it would probably be a good&nbsp;
idea for Dianne Feinstein to resign.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:00.840
What exactly the timing of that would be. And&nbsp;
this issue of the replacement versus getting back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:07.020
to the Senate Judiciary Committee, I don't know.&nbsp;
It's not about again, it's not about stigmatizing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:10.920
It's not about making fun of anyone. It's not&nbsp;
about any of these things. It's about political&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:16.500
expediency. And Feinstein has had an incredible&nbsp;
run in the Senate, has accomplished so much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:21.960
iconic in so many different ways. Nothing&nbsp;
is being taken away from her. In my mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:28.020
if she did resign. Republicans are jumping all&nbsp;
over this and saying she should not resign.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:33.540
And now Democrats are being bad in some way&nbsp;
by urging her to do so. This is, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:38.820
Republicans concerned only with self-preservation&nbsp;
and realizing that it's actually been a great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:45.240
thing for them that Joe Biden's judicial nominees&nbsp;
have been held up as a result of this. So I,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:49.680
